Nothing changed in the repository this run. The issue now waits on the hub's day of evidence. I committed nothing, landed nothing, and left the issue open.

- **Why it waits:** looper#173 (retrying build jobs that fail on infrastructure) merged and closed at 03:43Z. Jody's 03:01Z decision says this issue goes ahead only if image pulls still fail after a retry, counted over a day of build jobs. That day hasn't started: the hub still has to copy looper's `ci/build.gitlab-ci.yml` into tacplus-dev/build and unpause the in-cluster build runner.
- **What I did:** commented on the issue (https://github.com/tacplus-dev/cluster/issues/27#issuecomment-6937624366) asking the hub for one of two outcomes, and added `needs-decision`. There's no open issue I could name as the blocker, so I couldn't mark it `Blocked-by:` instead.
  - **No timeouts survive a retry:** the hub closes the issue, or lets me close it with their count as the evidence.
  - **Pulls still fail:** the hub removes `needs-decision` and I do option (b). Here that means a `mirror-images` job and its digest list. I'd also file an issue in cloud for image streaming on both pools and one in looper for pointing job images at the mirror. I asked the hub to post the before-and-after pull times too, since loopers can't see the cluster.
- **Checkpoint:** saved on `looper/cluster-27` with the same status. It reported "2 files changed, 185 insertions", although my checkout showed no changes at the start of the run. I didn't check which files those were.
